lines=['# Perpetual-specific strategy and execution study','','## Decision','','Perpetuals have usable liquidity and deserve a dedicated strategy design. Priority1: volatility-sized channel breakout, with SOL as the first research candidate and BTC/BCH as comparisons. Priority2: gold/silver relative-value reversal. Priority3: a measured maker-execution experiment on metals, not a claimed market-making profit. Keep the earlier LTC trend candidate as a comparator. There is no verified live edge from this short, repeatedly examined sample, and no trading system was activated.','','The earlier fixed6/24-hour strategy sweeps were incomplete coverage. This study adds75 event-driven directional variants,5 paired-ratio tests, all25 product economics, and60 fresh order-book snapshots. These new variants use stops, dynamic exits and whole-contract risk sizing. The records overlap earlier research, so the new tests are exploratory, not independent validation.','','## Liquidity and account facts','',f"Read-only authenticated /margin/enabled returned {account['enabled']}; fresh effective fees match the earlier receipt. Crypto maker/taker:2/12bp per side. Metals:0.12/0.72bp per side. One basis point is0.01%. Public snapshots show BTC reported24h notional volume about$117.9m and ETH$136.1m. Volume is executed turnover, not bankroll opportunity or expected profit. Public books provide current depth, not guaranteed future executions. Account access is confirmed; balances, collateral allocation and ability to execute a particular order were not tested.",'','For a$50 crypto position, taker fees are approximately12c round trip before spread/funding/slippage; metals about0.72c. Short-horizon crypto strategies must clear this hurdle repeatedly. Larger leveraged exposure scales fees and risk, not evidence of an edge.','','## Strategy1: volatility-sized channel breakout','','At each completed hour buy a breakout above the preceding24-hour midpoint high or short a break below its low. Exit an opposite12-hour channel break, a volatility stop, or the72-hour holding limit. Entry/exit execute at next-hour bid/ask closes. No best UTC clock is chosen. Stop distance is twice trailing hourly-return standard deviation scaled to one day; whole-contract size is capped at$50notional and$1estimated loss at the initial stop distance. The stop is a trigger, not a guaranteed price: observed hourly breach triggers next-hour exit. Gaps/fees can make losses exceed$1. Quotes need90% history coverage; omitted timestamps are not forward-filled.','','| Product | Trades | Net after all modeled costs | +5bp/side execution stress | Recent14day net | Observed hourly drawdown |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for t in ['SOL','BTC','BCH','LTC','ETH','XRP']:
 a=next(x for x in r if x['name']=='KX'+t+'PERP_channel24_12');lines.append(f"| {t} | {a['trades']} | ${a['net']:+.2f} | ${a['stress5']:+.2f} | ${a['recent']:+.2f} | ${a['drawdown']:.2f} |")
lines+=['','These are isolated strategy P&Ls at variable size <=$50, not additive gains on a single$100account. About49days of crypto history were available, and less for newer products. Missing hourly marks make drawdown incomplete; liquidation and native stop execution are not simulated. Tail risk can exceed this record.','','The largest winners across crypto occurred during the same August18–22 rally. XRP EMA’s+$25.64 total contains a single+$27.05 trade; without that one trade it loses. SOL breakout’s+$8.46 contains a+$7.67 winner; removing its top3 trades gives−$2.37. Breakout strategies naturally rely on occasional trends, but this sample cannot establish repeatability. Same-window long-only controls also exceed most trend results. These controls inherit strategy-selected windows and therefore are attribution diagnostics, not independently deployable buy-and-hold comparisons.','','| Channel product | Strategy | Long-only on identical windows/counts |','|---|---:|---:|']
for t in ['SOL','BTC','BCH','LTC','ETH','XRP']:
 a=controls['KX'+t+'PERP_channel24_12'];lines.append(f"| {t} | ${a['net']:+.2f} | ${a['same_windows_long']:+.2f} |")
lines+=['','Why SOL first: this is a research-priority judgment based on the measured balance of positive early/recent segments and lower observed drawdown, not a statistically established winner. Ranking after seeing80variants adds selection bias. We should freeze the rule and test forward, not optimize the August rally.','','## Strategy2: gold/silver relative value','','Compute the72-hour distribution of log(gold-perp price/silver-perp price). If its z-score exceeds+2, short gold and buy silver; reverse for−2. Freeze entry mean/standard deviation; exit at absolute z<=0.5, adverse/extreme absolute z>=4, or24hours. Equal nominal$25 per leg in whole contracts, one-hour execution delay, both legs’ fees/spreads/funding included. Dollar matching does not eliminate gold/silver economic, beta, or basis risk; paired orders are not atomic.','','| Pair | Trades | Net | +5bp/side | Hourly drawdown |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
