lines+=['','Gold/silver has about15days of product history and12trades; its+$0.68 becomes−$0.10 after removing the three best trades. This is a new low-cost paper candidate, not hedge arbitrage or guaranteed passive income. Crypto pairs generally fail after repeated fees.','','## Strategy3: market making and short-horizon execution','','12snapshots per asset over about27seconds measure immediate feasibility only. There are no historical queue-position/fill probabilities in this study. Buying at bid and selling at ask is a favorable two-maker-fill assumption, not a backtest.','','| Asset | Median displayed spread(bp) | Two maker fees(bp) | Spread less fees(bp) | Approx gross room on$50 before adverse selection |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
